#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:1 2caa9bd754b242b68ff19dda303fac1f
msgid "Slack-Based Efficiency: From Common Contraction to Specific Operating Gaps"
msgstr "基于松弛量的效率：从共同压缩到具体经营缺口"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:3 8eb5db3d7e954f34afa6ce32cef7b0b7
msgid ""
"At a hospital performance meeting, a result such as “no further common "
"percentage reduction in resources” can sound like the end of the "
"efficiency discussion. Yet the same comparison evidence may show excess "
"diagnostic capacity in one department and an attainable service gain in "
"another. The radial result is not wrong. It has answered a deliberately "
"compact question about one common proportional change; it has not claimed"
" that every resource--service gap has disappeared."
msgstr "在医院绩效会议上，“资源已无法再按共同百分比减少”这样的结果，听起来似乎已经结束了效率讨论。然而，同一比较证据可能同时表明某个科室诊断能力过剩，另一个科室仍可增加服务。径向结果并没有错；它有意回答的是一次共同比例调整这一简洁问题，从未声称每一项资源—服务缺口都已消失。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:11 beb4dad5fae440f680acaf23fe83b5ae
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Slack-based methods shift attention from a common percentage to the "
"particular resources and services that constrain performance. Diagnostic "
"capacity may be excessive even when nursing hours are not; one service "
"line may have room to expand while another already meets best observed "
"practice. The classic additive model, the range-adjusted measure (RAM), "
"and Tone's slacks-based measure (SBM) form one useful family for studying"
" such uneven opportunities {cite:p}`charnes1985,cooper1999,tone2001`. "
"They use the same kinds of feasible benchmark plans and expose the same "
"physical gaps, but summarize those gaps on different scales."
msgstr ""
"松弛测度把注意力从共同百分比转向制约绩效的具体资源与服务。即使护理工时并不过量，诊断能力仍可能过剩；某条服务线还可扩张，另一条却已达到观测到的最佳实践。经典加法模型、极差调整测度"
"（range-adjusted measure，RAM）和 Tone 的基于松弛变量的效率测度（slacks-based "
"measure，SBM）构成一个适合研究此类不均衡机会的模型族 "
"{cite:p}`charnes1985,cooper1999,tone2001`。它们采用同类可行标杆方案，也揭示同类物理缺口，但用不同标尺汇总这些缺口。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:20 a957f77a9c8f46528ff216d535f7ae2c
msgid ""
"That distinction is managerial, not merely algebraic. An original-unit "
"gap, a gap relative to the observed sample range, and a gap relative to "
"the focal organization's own operation answer different reporting "
"questions. None is a price, a welfare weight, or a universally valid "
"league-table score. The physical gaps and the assumptions that make them "
"feasible should therefore be understood before any aggregate number is "
"interpreted."
msgstr "这种区别具有管理含义，不只是代数差异。以原始单位表示的缺口、相对于观测样本极差的缺口，以及相对于被评价组织自身经营量的缺口，回答的是不同报告问题。任何一种都不是价格、福利权重或普遍有效的排行榜得分。因此，在解释汇总数值之前，应先理解各项物理缺口及使其可行的假设。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:27 5690d826406845b7afef8bd3c04b8716
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Part I established why the economic roles of the variables and the "
"eligibility of comparators must be settled in the "
"{doc}`../01-foundations/02-study-design`, and how production assumptions "
"define attainable practice in the {doc}`../01-foundations/02-production-"
"frontier`. Those choices remain unchanged here. Normalization merely "
"determines how several physical shortfalls contribute to one summary "
"measure. It cannot make unlike organizations comparable, turn an "
"irrelevant column into a legitimate input or output, or give managerial "
"importance to a gap that the study never justified."
msgstr ""
"第一部分已经说明，为何必须先在 {doc}`../01-foundations/02-study-design` "
"中确定变量的经济角色和比较对象资格，并在 {doc}`../01-foundations/02-production-frontier` "
"中用生产假设界定可实现实践。本章不改变这些选择。归一化只决定多个物理缺口如何进入一个汇总测度；它不能使原本不同的组织变得可比，不能把无关列变成合理的投入或产出，也不能赋予研究从未论证的缺口以管理重要性。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:36 e7bfa1383ba64ec68fca91ba2910d5ec
msgid "Begin with one feasible operating plan"
msgstr "从一个可行经营方案开始"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:38 5fc41678e88c48b199924cddb6d48dab
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Let organization $o$ use inputs $x_o\\in\\mathbb{R}_{+}^{m}$ to produce "
"desirable outputs $y_o\\in\\mathbb{R}_{+}^{s}$. A benchmark assembled "
"from the eligible reference population has intensity vector $\\lambda$. "
"Under the standard free-disposal account, one feasible comparison plan "
"can be written"
msgstr ""
"令组织 $o$ 使用投入 $x_o\\in\\mathbb{R}_{+}^{m}$ 生产合意产出 "
"$y_o\\in\\mathbb{R}_{+}^{s}$。由合格参照总体构造的标杆，其强度向量为 "
"$\\lambda$。在标准自由处置账户下，一个可行比较方案可写为"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:43 939a879e0d764aaaa9a45ff9953330ac
msgid ""
"\n"
"X\\lambda+s^-=x_o,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Y\\lambda-s^+=y_o,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\lambda,s^-,s^+\\geq0,\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"X\\lambda+s^-=x_o,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Y\\lambda-s^+=y_o,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\lambda,s^-,s^+\\geq0,\n"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:51 8a610935ae7e4fbfafda65a288d57d0d
msgid ""
"together with the chosen returns-to-scale restriction. The implied "
"operating targets are"
msgstr "并附加所选规模报酬约束。相应的经营目标为"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:54 51c8eb7639b841b993de4dce0067f4af
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\widehat x_o=x_o-s^-,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\widehat y_o=y_o+s^+.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\widehat x_o=x_o-s^-,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\widehat y_o=y_o+s^+.\n"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:60 7fb146f1fef54770a734cf75cbaf605b
msgid ""
"An input slack $s_i^-$ is a resource saving supported by the maintained "
"technology while the represented service commitments are protected. An "
"output slack $s_r^+$ is an attainable service addition without breaching "
"the represented resource limits. These are properties of a comparison "
"plan, not yet recommendations to close a ward, reduce a budget, or impose"
" a service quota."
msgstr ""
"投入松弛量 $s_i^-$ 表示：在保障代表性服务责任时，既定技术能够支持的资源节约。产出松弛量 $s_r^+$ "
"表示：在不突破代表性资源限额时可以实现的服务增加。这些是比较方案的性质，尚不是关闭病区、削减预算或规定服务配额的建议。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:67 7725afd0ee474908803d67a1c56b2e27
msgid ""
"The balance equations do not dictate how unlike gaps should be "
"aggregated. They supply a common physical ledger: the eligible "
"comparators, their weights, the original-unit gaps, and the implied "
"targets. A given feasible plan can be read with each of the rulers below."
" When the models are fitted separately, however, their different "
"objectives can select different feasible plans. The shared ledger is the "
"conceptual common ground, not a promise that every dataset will produce "
"identical peers or targets."
msgstr "这些平衡方程没有规定应如何汇总性质不同的缺口。它们提供一套共同的物理明细：合格比较对象及其权重、以原始单位表示的缺口和隐含目标方案。下面每种标尺都可以用来阅读同一个可行方案。不过，当各模型分别拟合时，不同目标函数可能选出不同的可行方案。共同的物理明细是概念上的共同基础，并不保证每个数据集都会得到相同的活跃参照单元或目标方案。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:75 61113723e4b3437ea482b1339ebb91b2
msgid "The same gaps under three reporting rulers"
msgstr "用三种报告标尺衡量同一类缺口"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:77 63b62bdf9aaa43a0ae5b0755a81e483c
msgid "The classic additive model maximizes the total physical gap"
msgstr "经典加法模型最大化物理缺口总量"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:79 68a3bc467fb443f09acae53865df402a
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\delta_o\n"
"=\\sum_{i=1}^{m}s_i^-+\\sum_{r=1}^{s}s_r^+,\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\delta_o\n"
"=\\sum_{i=1}^{m}s_i^-+\\sum_{r=1}^{s}s_r^+,\n"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:84 dbabb7843bcc490cae133b5dd57ce29c
msgid ""
"subject to the same input and output balances. In its original VRS, unit-"
"weight form, zero is best: $\\delta_o=0$ means that no represented "
"componentwise improvement remains. A positive optimum implies that at "
"least one resource excess or service shortfall remains; the associated "
"slack ledger, not the scalar total, identifies where it lies."
msgstr ""
"并满足相同的投入、产出平衡。在原始 VRS、单位权重形式下，零为最优值：$\\delta_o=0$ "
"表示所列变量中不再存在可以逐项实现的改进。正的最优值表示至少还有一项资源冗余或服务不足；具体位置应由配套的松弛量明细识别，而不是由标量总和识别。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:90 bdf168fa362d4212b1abed3317a22d82
msgid ""
"The physical slack table is highly informative, but the scalar sum has no"
" general percentage interpretation. Ten staff hours, two tonnes of "
"material, and five units of service do not become economically equivalent"
" merely because they enter one objective. Changing tonnes to kilograms "
"can change both the additive value and the selected target. The classic "
"additive account is therefore most informative as a search for a "
"componentwise-improved feasible plan and as an original-unit ledger. Its "
"raw total is not a universal ranking scale."
msgstr ""
"物理松弛量表很有信息价值，但其标量总和一般不能解释为百分比。10 个员工工时、2 吨材料和 5 "
"单位服务不会因为进入同一目标函数就变得经济等价。把吨换成千克，会同时改变加法数值和所选目标。经典加法账户因而最适合用来寻找逐项改善的可行方案，并提供原始单位明细；它的原始总量不是通用排序标尺。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:99 a1bfee06808043d89cce5eb7a9a83343
msgid ""
"RAM retains the variable-specific ledger but supplies a sample ruler. "
"Write the observed range of input $i$ as $R_i^x$ and that of output $r$ "
"as $R_r^y$. Under the VRS balances above, RAM selects the plan that "
"maximizes range-normalized slack and reports its higher-is-better "
"complement:"
msgstr ""
"RAM 保留逐变量明细，但增加一把样本标尺。记投入 $i$ 的观测极差为 $R_i^x$，产出 $r$ 的观测极差为 $R_r^y$。在上述 "
"VRS 平衡下，RAM 选择使极差归一化松弛量最大的方案，并报告其越高越好的补数："

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:104 6ae5667475d24c49baaf0e47c07a5f6a
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\delta_o^{RAM}\n"
"=\\max_{\\lambda,s^-,s^+}\\frac{1}{m+s}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\sum_{i:R_i^x>0}\\frac{s_i^-}{R_i^x}\n"
"+\\sum_{r:R_r^y>0}\\frac{s_r^+}{R_r^y}\n"
"\\right),\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\rho_o^{RAM}=1-\\delta_o^{RAM}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\delta_o^{RAM}\n"
"=\\max_{\\lambda,s^-,s^+}\\frac{1}{m+s}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\sum_{i:R_i^x>0}\\frac{s_i^-}{R_i^x}\n"
"+\\sum_{r:R_r^y>0}\\frac{s_r^+}{R_r^y}\n"
"\\right),\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\rho_o^{RAM}=1-\\delta_o^{RAM}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:115 94d18629f1664d0bb08678a1a891e823
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A contribution of 0.20 means “one fifth of this variable's observed "
"sample range,” not “a 20-percent cost saving.” The normalization removes "
"physical units, but the ruler exists only for variables with positive "
"sample ranges. An extreme observation can change the ruler as well as the"
" estimated production frontier. RAM is consequently a sample-relative "
"member of the same slack family, not an independent economic "
"interpretation "
"{cite:p}`cooper1999,steinmann2001ram,cooper2001ramresponse`."
msgstr ""
"某项贡献为 0.20，表示“该变量观测样本极差的五分之一”，而不是“成本节约 "
"20%”。归一化消除了物理单位，但只有样本极差为正的变量才有这种标尺。极端观测既可能改变标尺，也可能改变估计的生产前沿。因此，RAM "
"是同一松弛测度族中相对于样本的成员，并没有独立的经济解释 "
"{cite:p}`cooper1999,steinmann2001ram,cooper2001ramresponse`。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:123 e42d6681ae004e3f9feb87a55d8f9ba2
msgid ""
"The named RAM profile uses one self-inclusive VRS comparison and computes"
" each range from that same reference population. Because translating a "
"quantity translates the feasible balance without changing its range or "
"slack, RAM can also accommodate finite signed data. A coordinate with "
"zero range contributes zero to the normalized objective and, under the "
"matched VRS balance, cannot carry a nonzero slack. These are properties "
"of the RAM ruler, not permissions to shift standard SBM data by an "
"arbitrary constant."
msgstr ""
"具名 RAM 设定采用一个包含被评价单元自身的 VRS "
"比较，并从同一参照总体计算各项极差。平移某个数量时，可行平衡随之平移，而其极差和松弛量不变，因此 RAM "
"也可以处理有限的有符号数据。极差为零的坐标对归一化目标贡献为零，并且在匹配的 VRS 平衡下不能具有非零松弛量。这些是 RAM "
"标尺的性质，并不意味着可以给标准 SBM 数据任意加上常数。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:131 844687c6eed64334b1a4fdfed93f79bf
msgid ""
"SBM supplies an organization-specific ruler. For strictly positive inputs"
" and outputs, define the average proportional gaps"
msgstr "SBM 提供一把针对具体组织的标尺。对于严格为正的投入和产出，定义平均比例缺口"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:134 8cdf134f03164bd395e088bfbd271100
msgid ""
"\n"
"L_o^x=\\frac{1}{m}\\sum_{i=1}^{m}\\frac{s_i^-}{x_{io}},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"L_o^y=\\frac{1}{s}\\sum_{r=1}^{s}\\frac{s_r^+}{y_{ro}}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"L_o^x=\\frac{1}{m}\\sum_{i=1}^{m}\\frac{s_i^-}{x_{io}},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"L_o^y=\\frac{1}{s}\\sum_{r=1}^{s}\\frac{s_r^+}{y_{ro}}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:140 4efabb9d99eb4eec84696e200d939778
msgid ""
"Each gap is now judged relative to the quantity facing the focal "
"organization. Suppose two clinics could each release ten employees while "
"maintaining their services. Ten employees are half of a 20-person "
"workforce but only one percent of a 1,000-person workforce. An absolute "
"slack records the same physical gap; SBM records very different "
"proportional burdens."
msgstr ""
"此时，每项缺口都相对于被评价组织所面对的数量来判断。假设两家诊所都能在维持服务的同时减少 10 名员工。10 人是一家 20 "
"人机构的一半，却只是一家 1,000 人机构的 1%。绝对松弛量记录相同的物理缺口，SBM 记录的相对负担却大不相同。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 825ab2a2b34a484b8e977dfa62cdc651
msgid ""
"The same input slack of ten is a large proportional gap for a small unit "
"and a small proportional gap for a large unit"
msgstr "同样为 10 的投入松弛量，对小型组织是很大的比例缺口，对大型组织则很小"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:151 123ce91e5f574ba4934d943f5259cd00
msgid ""
"Own-observation normalization asks how large an operating gap is relative"
" to the activity that faces it."
msgstr "以本组织观测量归一化，是在考察经营缺口相对于承担该缺口的生产活动有多大。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:155 3f0e63b6d9de4a6c97a264e32e91cfd1
msgid ""
"This normalization is dimensionless and unit invariant. Changing "
"employees to thousands of employees, or pounds to millions of pounds, "
"scales the observation and its slack together. It does **not** make one "
"employee, one bed, and one pound equally valuable in an economic sense. "
"The standard average assigns equal weight to each represented dimension; "
"variable selection is therefore part of the performance judgement. This "
"is a measurement convention, not a system of prices or social values."
msgstr "这种归一化没有量纲，并具有单位不变性。把员工数改用千人为单位，或把英镑改用百万英镑为单位，观测值与松弛量会同时缩放。它**不**表示一名员工、一张病床和一英镑在经济上具有相同价值。标准平均对每个代表性维度赋予相同权重，因此变量选择本身就是绩效判断的一部分。这是一项测量约定，不是价格体系或社会价值体系。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:163 38a9166266d0481c8457ea4f6b9f3e28
msgid ""
"For example, suppose a provider has two inputs. Its benchmark identifies "
"a 20-percent staffing excess but no excess in capital. The average "
"proportional input gap is 10 percent, so its input-oriented score is "
"0.90. The conclusion is not “cut every input by 10 percent.” It is that "
"one input has a specific 20-percent gap and the equal-dimension account "
"averages it with a zero gap in the other input. Whenever management is "
"expected to act, the variable-level diagnosis must accompany the average."
msgstr ""
"例如，某服务机构有两项投入。其标杆识别出人员投入过量 20%，资本却没有过量。平均比例投入缺口为 10%，所以投入导向得分为 "
"0.90。结论并不是“每项投入都削减 10%”，而是一项投入有明确的 20% "
"缺口，等维度账户把它与另一项投入的零缺口取平均。只要结果可能用于管理行动，就必须在平均值之外同时报告逐变量诊断。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:171 9264e4aa99704771a6f7dadad94a043f
msgid ""
"The three rulers can now be compared without mistaking them for three "
"separate production technologies:"
msgstr "现在可以比较三种标尺，而不会误以为它们代表三种不同生产技术："

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 9df48bc30f4b426b8e269585d76fb7ce
msgid "Ruler"
msgstr "标尺"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 a172b981a9ad461f8f32475d3f69ecb2
msgid "What a gap is compared with"
msgstr "缺口与什么比较"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 6296d4a82c2a4009a7e421869cf1da7f
msgid "Main interpretive boundary"
msgstr "主要解释边界"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 866776a4b41e439cb7c9b4504ce093bb
msgid "Additive"
msgstr "加法模型"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 979635efedb54912ae4791d490109066
msgid "Its original physical unit and declared weights"
msgstr "缺口原有的物理单位与预先声明的权重"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 b383e6682cbe4c1a807a815f6d9470c7
msgid "Unlike units cannot be added into a universal percentage"
msgstr "单位不同的数量不能相加成通用百分比"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 64210cf6ffeb49ea84827a8c7e090ddb
msgid "RAM"
msgstr "RAM"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 42acc6479213425698e262ca48a02a6b
msgid "Full variation in the declared sample"
msgstr "所声明样本中的全部变异范围"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 8e2f13aca92c4533be04e80ee5a6d293
msgid "Scores change when the sample ruler changes"
msgstr "样本标尺变化时，得分也会变化"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 dd592ff469f042a7b3a1d0e6474e6cf1
msgid "SBM"
msgstr "SBM"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 67a5afa228014924a48eedaa3763faf7
msgid "The focal organization's own quantity"
msgstr "被评价组织自身的数量"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 6baf59f2e69f4f318f0f7ab669db3c93
msgid "Zeros and translations change or invalidate the ratio account"
msgstr "零值和平移会改变比例账户，或使其失效"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:180 6e4d897595da4e8d9fabf933d381cca4
msgid ""
"An additive slack account may use pre-declared positive weights, but they"
" change how feasible improvements are valued and may change the target. "
"The standard RAM and SBM accounts used here retain their defining equal-"
"dimension normalizations. A conversion factor, an observed price, and a "
"stakeholder priority are not interchangeable. When expenditure, revenue, "
"or profit is the real question, the price-based economic-efficiency "
"models later in this part provide the clearer account."
msgstr ""
"加法松弛账户可以采用预先声明的正权重，但这些权重会改变可行改进的价值评价，也可能改变目标方案。本章使用的标准 RAM 和 SBM "
"账户保留各自定义中的等维度归一化。换算因子、观测价格和利益相关者优先级不能互换。当真正的问题是支出、收益或利润时，本部分稍后的价格型经济效率模型会提供更清楚的账户。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:188 0d16eaf63f0a4263b16b5428e12296a5
msgid ""
"An advanced bridge: a declared compromise between common change and input"
" mix"
msgstr "进阶桥梁：在共同调整与投入组合之间作出明确折中"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:190 f6c79abc06084677afbd1283e5b7caf1
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Some management settings do not want either a purely common contraction "
"or an equal treatment of every input gap. EBM offers a disciplined "
"compromise: one term records the common input factor and another records "
"an importance-weighted input mix {cite:p}`tone2010ebm`. The two terms use"
" one joint peer plan, so the result is neither an average of a radial "
"score and an SBM score nor a claim that the same resource adjustment is "
"sensible in every service system."
msgstr ""
"有些管理场景既不希望采用纯粹的共同压缩，也不希望平等对待每项投入缺口。EBM "
"提供一种规范的折中：一项记录共同投入因子，另一项记录按重要性加权的投入组合 "
"{cite:p}`tone2010ebm`。两项使用同一个联合参照方案，所以结果既不是径向得分与 SBM "
"得分的平均，也不主张同一资源调整适合每种服务系统。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:197 3aa989e5f5c446c28d46e174c4267dbb
msgid ""
"This book treats that compromise as advanced because the importance "
"calibration is part of the decision, not a harmless software setting. "
"DEAPack's public EBM evaluator requires the analyst to declare the "
"calibration and its provenance before fitting. It can consequently "
"support a transparent question such as: given a committee's documented "
"view of the relative importance of physician and nursing inputs, what "
"jointly feasible resource-and-input-mix adjustment is demonstrated by "
"comparable providers? It does not estimate those priorities from the "
"data."
msgstr ""
"本书把这种折中视为进阶内容，因为重要性校准本身是一项决策，而不是无关紧要的软件设置。DEAPack 的公开 EBM "
"评价器要求分析者在拟合前声明校准及其来源。因此，它可以透明地回答这样的问题：根据委员会有记录的医生与护理投入相对重要性判断，可比服务机构表明哪些资源用量与投入组合的联合调整可行？它不会从数据中估计这些优先级。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:206 e433703517324227a223c2209b8ecb58
msgid ""
"This matters for interpretation. The input-oriented source programme "
"allows substitution: a target can reduce one resource while increasing "
"another and still preserve the reported service commitments. That is a "
"possible operating mix under the stated technology, not a recommendation "
"to increase every input. At its radial endpoint the EBM score agrees with"
" matched CCR input efficiency; at its other endpoint it is still not "
"automatically an SBM, because the radial factor remains free. The "
"automatic affinity/PCA calibration discussed in the original article is "
"deliberately not run in this release. Readers who need the declared-"
"calibration evaluator and its certificates can use the package "
"Documentation; it is a supporting advanced tool, not a fourth ruler for "
"the core comparison above."
msgstr ""
"这一点直接影响解释。原文所定义的投入导向规划允许替代：在保障所报告服务责任的同时，目标方案可以减少一项资源而增加另一项。这是在所述技术下可能实现的经营组合，不是增加所有投入的建议。在径向端点，EBM"
" 得分与匹配的 CCR 投入效率一致；在另一端点，它也不会自动变成 SBM，因为径向因子仍是自由的。本版本有意不运行原文讨论的自动 "
"affinity/PCA 校准。需要使用声明式校准评价器及其证书的读者，可以查阅包 "
"Documentation；它是辅助性的进阶工具，不是上述核心比较的第四把标尺。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:218 22f82fecc7134fc19d39079b068060a9
msgid "One operating plan, three reporting rulers"
msgstr "一个经营方案，三把报告标尺"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:220 e1366c2e1ac8452f930682d4479ec4a1
msgid ""
"The difference among the three rulers is easiest to understand when the "
"physical benchmark is held fixed. The durable lesson is not to memorize "
"three historically named recipes. These appraisals belong in one slack "
"family because they use the same production account and ask for the same "
"kind of variable-specific improvement; the substantive difference here is"
" the ruler used to communicate that evidence."
msgstr "当物理标杆保持不变时，最容易看清三种标尺之间的区别。真正值得掌握的不是三套带有历史名称的公式。三种评价属于同一个松弛测度族，因为它们采用相同的生产账户，询问同类逐变量改进；这里有实质意义的区别，是用哪一把标尺传达这些证据。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:227 9702c5f765354d2fb681695a6422a4b9
msgid ""
"In the `slacks_2x2` teaching data, organization E uses labor and capital "
"to provide service and quality. The classic additive, RAM, and non-"
"oriented SBM appraisals all select the same VRS reference activity:"
msgstr ""
"在 `slacks_2x2` 教学数据中，组织 E 使用劳动和资本提供服务与质量。经典加法模型、RAM 和非导向 SBM 都选中同一个 VRS "
"参照生产活动："

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:231 48b2a678f9524356a93233a0be5b24ce
msgid ""
"\n"
"0.25B+0.75C.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"0.25B+0.75C.\n"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:235 0cb9d0299f7c49cd9a61ac156da80e30
msgid ""
"That activity supports exactly the same variable-level operating evidence"
" in all three fits: no labor saving, a capital saving of 1.125, a service"
" gain of 0.600, and a quality gain of 0.260. The common plan lets us "
"change only the reporting ruler rather than confusing a different score "
"with a different benchmark."
msgstr ""
"在三次拟合中，该生产活动都支持完全相同的逐变量经营证据：劳动节约为零，资本节约 1.125，服务增加 0.600，质量增加 "
"0.260。共同方案使我们能够只改变报告标尺，而不会把不同得分误当成不同标杆。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 5faf2928ba564a3883ad43d0b6619a98
msgid "Model report for E"
msgstr "E 的模型报告"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 e7d21ec521e240998b3ec3e01a789499
msgid "Value"
msgstr "数值"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 9f7210e0740c4a8f97b6efe5ad915d2e
msgid "Best value and direction"
msgstr "最优值与方向"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 bdf6b281614349ffb2df86c849f25ca8
msgid "What supplies the ruler?"
msgstr "标尺来自哪里？"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 3567b6ad2108438d8ef19c2fa3deeb5f
msgid "Additive weighted slack total"
msgstr "加法模型的加权松弛总量"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 59cfadd955cb49d4889c9d1656d58598
msgid "1.985000"
msgstr "1.985000"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 01014e736a1248128205a2b1a83baac7
msgid "0; lower is closer"
msgstr "0；越低越接近最优"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 b4bfc17537e34cacb9e60d2a00221a1d
msgid "The declared original-unit slack weights"
msgstr "以原始单位声明的松弛权重"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 399fea02aaf4485fb42cf174b24a875f
msgid "RAM efficiency"
msgstr "RAM 效率"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 43a1e7b57ce64ed29d9e088533f36541
msgid "0.506250"
msgstr "0.506250"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 7c54011886b24cf1a16422ec1e5af209
#: d6e7115f621f45a18880fb581f83e790
msgid "1; higher is closer"
msgstr "1；越高越接近最优"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 99b263dbf38047929da9c8abc17743a7
msgid "Each variable's range in the declared sample"
msgstr "所声明样本中各变量的极差"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 c0eae6c42b644b9782d902c145ce01f1
msgid "SBM efficiency"
msgstr "SBM 效率"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 5b651cfd30a1448a8670e87ea5b5494a
msgid "0.554763"
msgstr "0.554763"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:146 29e8f6a90b0c45788e920a7908e880f6
msgid "E's own observed quantity for each variable"
msgstr "E 各变量自身的观测量"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:288 403d51ad1aa64d9796c8c8ddc86c23fb
msgid ""
"The arithmetic makes the source of the disagreement visible. With unit "
"additive weights, the original-unit total is"
msgstr "算术关系清楚显示了分歧的来源。采用单位加法权重时，原始单位总量为"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:291 c95678763fe74a4f9c733881f64d377f
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\delta_E=0+1.125+0.600+0.260=1.985.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\delta_E=0+1.125+0.600+0.260=1.985.\n"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:295 eb66ae3863104fd281510f5c8de5085f
msgid ""
"The four sample ranges for labor, capital, service, and quality are 2.4, "
"2.0, 1.0, and 0.32. RAM therefore reports"
msgstr "劳动、资本、服务和质量的四个样本极差分别为 2.4、2.0、1.0 和 0.32。因此，RAM 报告"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:298 d813e233dbd24696bb34e2ef5f88a6ae
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\rho_E^{RAM}\n"
"=1-\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\frac{0}{2.4}+\\frac{1.125}{2.0}\n"
"+\\frac{0.600}{1.0}+\\frac{0.260}{0.32}\n"
"\\right)\n"
"=0.506250.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\rho_E^{RAM}\n"
"=1-\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\frac{0}{2.4}+\\frac{1.125}{2.0}\n"
"+\\frac{0.600}{1.0}+\\frac{0.260}{0.32}\n"
"\\right)\n"
"=0.506250.\n"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:308 8b61c56b107d486caa65fff9bb4e6b7f
msgid "SBM replaces those sample ranges by E's own observed quantities:"
msgstr "SBM 则用 E 自身的观测量取代这些样本极差："

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:310 5ce5eb9766454a80be7da31e0eff0469
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\rho_E^{NO}\n"
"=\\frac{\n"
"1-\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{0}{2.0}+\\frac{1.125}{2.8}\\right)\n"
"}{\n"
"1+\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{0.600}{1.3}+\\frac{0.260}{0.62}\\right)\n"
"}\n"
"=0.554763.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\rho_E^{NO}\n"
"=\\frac{\n"
"1-\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{0}{2.0}+\\frac{1.125}{2.8}\\right)\n"
"}{\n"
"1+\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{0.600}{1.3}+\\frac{0.260}{0.62}\\right)\n"
"}\n"
"=0.554763.\n"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:320 484abf0a888941c799c881d21531a6f8
msgid ""
"No new production opportunity enters these calculations. The denominators"
" change what the same four gaps mean in the final report."
msgstr "这些计算没有引入任何新的生产机会。分母改变的只是如何在最终报告中理解同样的四项缺口。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:323 97e8304d24ed478c87dc424f8368b854
msgid ""
"The comparison is meaningful because all three selected plans are "
"feasible under the same VRS technology and each observed--slack--target "
"identity closes. The figure also confirms that the three models select "
"the same physical plan in this example. The exact numerical checks are "
"documented separately in the DEAPack Documentation."
msgstr ""
"这一比较之所以有意义，是因为三个所选方案在同一 VRS "
"技术下均可行，而且每个“观测量—松弛量—目标量”恒等式都能闭合。图形还确认，本例的三个模型选择了同一个物理方案。精确数值检查另见 DEAPack "
"Documentation。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:329 64416bf3469d49c88f2b4e4ea968a1bf
msgid ""
"Organization E has the same VRS peers, original-unit slacks, and selected"
" targets under Additive DEA, RAM, and SBM, while three separate score "
"cards show their different model-specific rulers, best values, and "
"directions"
msgstr ""
"对组织 E，Additive DEA、RAM 与 SBM 得到相同的 VRS "
"活跃参照单元、原始单位松弛量和所选目标；三个独立得分卡则显示各模型不同的标尺、最优值与方向"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:334 2034c5b0867d4d9a8826a72d4288ac19
msgid ""
"One selected operating plan viewed through three reporting rulers. The "
"ledger keeps unlike resources and services in their original units. The "
"separate cards deliberately avoid a common score axis because the "
"additive total, RAM efficiency, and SBM efficiency do not measure "
"distance on one interchangeable scale."
msgstr ""
"用三把报告标尺观察一个所选经营方案。明细表使性质不同的资源和服务保留各自原始单位。不同得分卡有意不共用得分轴，因为加法总量、RAM 效率和 SBM"
" 效率并不是同一可互换尺度上的距离。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:341 f3c74dddd30e49daa59f7c765d45f962
msgid ""
"This agreement should not be promoted into a theorem. The three "
"objectives can select different optimal plans in another dataset, and "
"alternate optima can support the same score. Here the shared plan "
"isolates the transferable lesson: **1.985, 0.506250, and 0.554763 are "
"three model-specific reports of the same physical evidence, not competing"
" estimates of one universal efficiency percentage.** They cannot be "
"compared as if the larger number always indicated the better "
"organization, and their difference is not a robustness ranking."
msgstr ""
"这种一致不能被提升为定理。在其他数据中，三个目标函数可能选择不同的最优方案；多个最优解也可能支持同一得分。本例的共同方案用于揭示一个可迁移的教训：**1.985、0.506250"
" 和 0.554763 "
"是同一物理证据的三种模型特定报告，并不是同一个通用效率百分比的竞争性估计。**不能假定数值越大就总表示组织越好，它们之间的差异也不是稳健性排序。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:349 5b4628275d734c5e9470554186409f98
msgid ""
"The management report should therefore lead with the common capital "
"saving and service and quality gains. It should add the score whose ruler"
" matches the study purpose and state that ruler explicitly. The additive "
"total preserves a declared weighted physical-gap account, RAM locates "
"gaps relative to the sample's spread, and SBM locates them relative to "
"E's own operation. None of those normalizations turns the selected plan "
"into a budget instruction or a causal explanation."
msgstr ""
"因此，管理报告应首先说明共同的资本节约、服务增加和质量增加，再根据研究目的选择标尺匹配的得分，并明确说明这把标尺。加法总量保留预先声明的加权物理缺口账户，RAM"
" 相对于样本离散范围定位缺口，SBM 则相对于 E 自身经营量定位缺口。任何一种归一化都不会把所选方案变成预算指令或因果解释。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:357 f34d2e6c49794b39aa581b9d952b153f
msgid "One SBM family, three management mandates"
msgstr "一个 SBM 模型族，三种管理任务"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:359 89128901f92748f2a6cf2b93c806c59b
msgid ""
"Once the own-operation ruler has been chosen, orientation determines "
"which gaps define the formal performance account. All three mainstream "
"orientations use the same production technology and the same kind of "
"feasible balance, but they encode different assignments of managerial "
"responsibility:"
msgstr "一旦选择以本组织自身经营量作为标尺，导向便决定哪些缺口构成正式绩效账户。三种主流导向采用同一个生产技术和同类可行平衡，但编码了不同的管理责任分工："

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:329 5c228dc7cdd243448109735f3b5c4ae1
msgid "Management mandate"
msgstr "管理任务"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:329 f0a57eab0eab460b909ff29573d923c6
msgid "Resources"
msgstr "资源"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:329 e50cc89acbbc4d96a6993477fc26a80d
msgid "Services"
msgstr "服务"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:329 f69af5b9d66944f4b1cf44fa30147813
msgid "DEAPack estimator"
msgstr "DEAPack 估计器"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:329 67cdd42e9e5041aca29673b4558dd77b
msgid "Conserve resources"
msgstr "节约资源"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:329 1cccc0a83cd54887ba4280ad66264e87
#: c49da761683540f9a21ffad615005771
msgid "May fall separately"
msgstr "可以分别减少"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:329 6d80c17369c241f6ab7c085e0a6183e8
msgid "May not fall"
msgstr "不得减少"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:329 abd861e2d6404e7f8bcdf33b0c32d1c5
msgid "`InputSBM`"
msgstr "`InputSBM`"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:329 141dda97bbf6442e983c45986b8a76ac
msgid "Expand services"
msgstr "扩张服务"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:329 39905bb3e52446bd8f32a7d59c10db7b
msgid "May not rise"
msgstr "不得增加"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:329 4cbf7769d70246188d8f4c0a44a11bb6
#: 9f9c8326ed2b4d37bb364c6a157e3473
msgid "May rise separately"
msgstr "可以分别增加"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:329 f9e613f776c64da685898972f1e0182b
msgid "`OutputSBM`"
msgstr "`OutputSBM`"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:329 7b79e91122984b8e85e6975d6826da2b
msgid "Redesign operations jointly"
msgstr "联合重构经营方案"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:329 1116e2c1a8c243b69f46301a9c0bf748
msgid "`SBM`"
msgstr "`SBM`"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:370 8a4b371ec5db462e873d59680bea27fe
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Several historical names collapse into these same contracts on the "
"standard strictly positive, equal-dimension-weighted domain: the input "
"Russell measure is input-oriented SBM, the output Russell expansion "
"account is reported through the reciprocal output-oriented SBM score, and"
" the enhanced Russell graph (ERG) measure is non-oriented SBM. These are "
"conditional aliases, not additional model families; other Russell graph, "
"weighted, closest-target, or signed-data formulations require separate "
"definitions and remain in the technical Documentation {cite:p}`tone2001`."
msgstr ""
"在标准的严格正值、等维度加权定义域上，多个历史名称归入这些相同契约：投入 Russell 测度就是投入导向 SBM；产出 Russell "
"扩张账户通过产出导向 SBM 得分的倒数来报告；增强 Russell 图（enhanced Russell graph，ERG）测度就是非导向 "
"SBM。它们是有条件成立的别名，不是额外模型族；其他 Russell 图、加权、最近目标或有符号数据形式需要另行定义，并保留在技术 "
"Documentation 中 {cite:p}`tone2001`。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:379 a2f92f6b8ff3472092fad659b88a22df
msgid ""
"Three management mandates use the same production technology to conserve "
"resources, expand services, or redesign both sides jointly"
msgstr "三种管理任务使用同一个生产技术，分别考察资源节约、服务扩张或两侧联合重构"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:384 045e7bf685f44f838f020d4e78d8979f
msgid ""
"Orientation is a statement about decision authority. It determines which "
"operating improvements define performance; it is not merely a "
"computational setting."
msgstr "导向表达的是决策权限。它决定哪些经营改进构成绩效，而不仅是一个计算设置。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:389 1806027263af4526bb1630cfa6023859
msgid ""
"An input orientation is appropriate when service obligations must be "
"maintained and management is accountable for resource stewardship. An "
"output orientation fits a capacity-constrained provider asked to increase"
" delivery. The non-oriented model fits an operational redesign in which "
"both sides may change. Their feasible plans come from one production "
"account, but their objectives need not select the same plan. Estimating "
"all three can show whether a conclusion depends on the mandate; it should"
" not become a search for the orientation that produces the most "
"convenient ranking."
msgstr "当服务义务必须维持、管理层对资源使用负责时，投入导向较为合适；当服务机构受产能约束、任务是增加供给时，产出导向更合适；当两侧都允许改变时，非导向模型适合经营重构。它们的可行方案来自同一个生产账户，但各自目标不一定选中同一方案。同时估计三个导向可以说明结论是否依赖所评价的管理任务，却不应变成寻找最方便排序的导向。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:398 38bd30d177434fcb9a86b44a6381c397
msgid "Input-oriented SBM: how much resource burden can be released?"
msgstr "投入导向 SBM：可以释放多少资源负担？"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:400 eeb6e63dafb2473e940ae80a8159821b
msgid "The input-oriented score is"
msgstr "投入导向得分为"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:402 a46ff25805b04539837abb7eff74ed70
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\rho_o^I=1-L_o^x\n"
"=1-\\frac{1}{m}\\sum_i\\frac{s_i^-}{x_{io}}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\rho_o^I=1-L_o^x\n"
"=1-\\frac{1}{m}\\sum_i\\frac{s_i^-}{x_{io}}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:407 02d536f22c5748b580bed54d39e7a0c8
msgid ""
"Minimizing $\\rho_o^I$ finds the greatest average proportional input "
"saving while the benchmark continues to produce at least the observed "
"outputs. A score of 0.80 means that the selected plan retains, on "
"average, 80 percent of the observed inputs after identified excesses are "
"removed. It does not mean that every input should be cut by 20 percent."
msgstr ""
"最小化 $\\rho_o^I$，是在标杆继续提供至少等于观测产出的条件下，寻找最大的平均比例投入节约。得分 0.80 "
"表示，所选方案去除已识别冗余后，平均保留观测投入的 80%。它不表示每项投入都应削减 20%。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:413 611d552ce1504704b71ea880c695ce54
msgid ""
"Output slacks may be feasible, but they do not define this score. The "
"model is answering a resource-stewardship question, not simultaneously "
"optimizing a service-expansion programme."
msgstr "产出松弛量可能可行，但不构成这一得分。模型回答的是资源使用责任问题，不会同时优化一套服务扩张方案。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:417 c5378f4f7fee4e8e98f58c81046984a6
msgid "Output-oriented SBM: how much service remains attainable?"
msgstr "产出导向 SBM：还能实现多少服务？"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:419 e470bbacecf941c78df76868109fc29e
msgid ""
"The output-oriented model uses the expansion account $1+L_o^y$ and "
"reports its higher-is-better reciprocal:"
msgstr "产出导向模型采用扩张账户 $1+L_o^y$，并报告其越高越好的倒数："

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:422 05a3744f030c4d69858a99269d0062e7
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\rho_o^O\n"
"=\\frac{1}{1+L_o^y}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{1+\\frac{1}{s}\\sum_r s_r^+/y_{ro}}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\rho_o^O\n"
"=\\frac{1}{1+L_o^y}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{1+\\frac{1}{s}\\sum_r s_r^+/y_{ro}}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:428 2165f3783a604fc7828a648905eaceda
msgid ""
"A score below one indicates that outputs can expand separately without "
"using more of any input. Because the denominator averages variable-"
"specific gains, this is not a common radial expansion factor. Input "
"savings may occur in a feasible solution, but they do not define the "
"output-oriented score."
msgstr ""
"得分低于 1 "
"表示，在不增加任何投入时，各项产出可以分别扩张。由于分母平均的是逐变量增加量，这不是共同径向扩张因子。可行解中可能出现投入节约，但它不构成产出导向得分。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:433 caf24d2996cf4f518e4d7c6bce7ebea6
msgid "Non-oriented SBM: what joint redesign is attainable?"
msgstr "非导向 SBM：能够实现怎样的联合重构？"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:435 3f1f5aa170f7478b9e7ec0aa5c543cd8
msgid ""
"When both resource conservation and service expansion belong to the "
"mandate, SBM combines the two accounts:"
msgstr "当管理任务同时包含资源节约与服务扩张时，SBM 把两个账户组合起来："

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:438 1b863392da7949c9a3e9c46a5247d925
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\rho_o^{NO}\n"
"=\\frac{1-L_o^x}{1+L_o^y}\n"
"=\\frac{\n"
"1-\\frac{1}{m}\\sum_i s_i^-/x_{io}\n"
"}{\n"
"1+\\frac{1}{s}\\sum_r s_r^+/y_{ro}\n"
"}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\rho_o^{NO}\n"
"=\\frac{1-L_o^x}{1+L_o^y}\n"
"=\\frac{\n"
"1-\\frac{1}{m}\\sum_i s_i^-/x_{io}\n"
"}{\n"
"1+\\frac{1}{s}\\sum_r s_r^+/y_{ro}\n"
"}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:448 32849568093c4d50be53deada005fba5
msgid ""
"The numerator and denominator should still be reported separately. A "
"joint score of 0.80 is not simply 20 percent too much input, 20 percent "
"too little output, or a 20 percent profit loss. It can combine a modest "
"resource excess with a larger service shortfall."
msgstr ""
"仍应分别报告分子和分母。联合得分 0.80 并不简单表示投入多了 20%、产出少了 20%，或利润损失 "
"20%；它可能由较小的资源冗余与较大的服务不足共同形成。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:453 9ddaeb202f5141e1a9720c672b2722f5
msgid ""
"With a self-inclusive reference population and the standard positive-data"
" technology, the non-oriented score equals one exactly when all input and"
" output slacks are zero. It can therefore certify strong, Pareto--"
"Koopmans efficiency for this account. A one-sided score of one certifies "
"only the mandate that was optimized."
msgstr ""
"在包含被评价单元自身的参照总体和标准正值技术下，非导向得分等于 1，当且仅当所有投入与产出松弛量均为零。因此，它可以认证该账户下的 Pareto"
"--Koopmans 强效率。单侧得分为 1，只能认证相应已优化的管理任务。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:459 e5e59f192ad94352953a1ecc7f61694f
msgid "Keep radial, slack, and directional claims distinct"
msgstr "区分径向、松弛量与方向性主张"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:461 cfc12c30b581407489381bd67c621f15
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The three model families can use the same empirical production technology"
" while describing different operating commitments. The {doc}`03"
"-classical-radial` asks for one common proportional contraction or "
"expansion and then may complete the selected plan with variable-specific "
"slacks. Additive, RAM, and SBM make those separate gaps the primary "
"performance evidence. A radial factor can therefore be one even when a "
"slack-based comparison still identifies a particular resource saving or "
"service gain {cite:p}`farrell1957,charnes1978`."
msgstr ""
"三个模型族可以使用同一个经验生产技术，却描述不同的经营承诺。{doc}`03-classical-radial` "
"要求投入或产出按一个共同比例压缩或扩张，随后可以用逐变量松弛量补全所选方案。加法模型、RAM 和 SBM "
"则把这些分别变化的缺口作为主要绩效证据。因此，即使径向因子为 1，松弛量比较仍可能识别某项具体资源节约或服务增加 "
"{cite:p}`farrell1957,charnes1978`。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:470 5f34f1ba82e147d98ea781cf637bfde2
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The {doc}`05-directional-distance` instead asks how many units of a "
"**pre-declared** resource-saving and service-expansion package are "
"feasible. Its single $\\beta$ forces the first-stage changes in that "
"package to move together in the proportions specified by the direction. "
"Non-oriented SBM does something different: its input and output gaps may "
"vary separately, and its score combines their average own-operation "
"proportions. Even when a DDF direction is constructed from the observed "
"quantities, the resulting $\\beta$ is not a relabelled SBM score "
"{cite:p}`chambers1996,tone2001`."
msgstr ""
"{doc}`05-directional-distance` 问的是：预先声明的一揽子资源节约与服务扩张方案能够实现多少单位。单一 "
"$\\beta$ 要求该方案第一阶段的各项变化按方向规定的比例共同调整。非导向 SBM "
"则不同：投入和产出缺口可以分别变化，得分汇总的是它们相对于本组织经营量的平均比例。即使 DDF 方向取自观测数量，所得 $\\beta$ "
"也不是换名后的 SBM 得分 {cite:p}`chambers1996,tone2001`。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:479 23d37982a1da4e6dbfaa1d13829e273c
msgid ""
"The practical choice follows the decision. Use a radial account when a "
"common percentage change is the relevant commitment, a DDF when "
"management has declared a bundled improvement programme, and a slack "
"account when the study must diagnose uneven opportunities across "
"represented resources and services. These are different estimands, not "
"competing algorithms in a race to produce the lowest or highest score."
msgstr ""
"实际选择取决于决策问题。共同百分比变化符合管理承诺时采用径向账户；管理层已经声明一揽子改进方案时采用 "
"DDF；研究需要诊断各项代表性资源和服务中的不均衡机会时采用松弛量账户。三者是不同的被估量，而不是竞相给出最低或最高得分的算法。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:486 a693202b32dd4dfcbaeca2e809ec244e
msgid "Why orientation changes the conclusion"
msgstr "为何导向会改变结论"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:488 c437267e7ccb4859add9183aa2d4bdb1
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The bundled `sbm_slack_contrast` dataset contains project-authored "
"neutral service plans with two inputs and two outputs. One compact "
"workflow fits the three mandates to the same CRS technology. Tone's "
"equations define the method {cite:p}`tone2001`; the package example does "
"not reproduce his table:"
msgstr ""
"内置的 `sbm_slack_contrast` 数据集包含项目自主编制的中性服务方案，设有两项投入和两项产出。一个简洁工作流把三种管理任务拟合到同一 "
"CRS 技术。Tone 的方程界定了这一方法 {cite:p}`tone2001`；包内示例并不复现其原表："

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:528 cd838514c81942348b858c69777a6c33
msgid ""
"The three columns apply distinct resource, service, and joint mandates to"
" the same observations. Inspect `scores` rather than expecting identical "
"rankings: a plan can have no supported input saving while retaining an "
"output shortfall, or the reverse. The non-oriented account combines both "
"sides through the SBM fraction defined above."
msgstr ""
"三列对同一组观测分别施加资源节约、服务扩张和联合改进任务。应查看 `scores`，不要预期三种排序完全相同：一个方案可能不存在得到标杆支持的投入节约，却仍有产出不足；反之亦然。非导向账户通过上文定义的 SBM 分式把投入和产出两侧结合起来。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:534 f54974c6094248f8a30d8e5aebdf5e46
msgid "The result can turn that account into a single management-facing display:"
msgstr "结果对象可以把这一账户转化为一幅面向管理的图："

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:543 4b9eaccd525842a9bda3fa6b44faaa8d
msgid ""
"The uneven service plan's selected SBM account displays variable-specific"
" resource savings and service gains together with original and target "
"quantities"
msgstr "不均衡服务方案所选的 SBM 账户同时展示逐变量资源节约与服务增加，以及观测量和目标量"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:548 4b9eaccd525842a9bda3fa6b44faaa8d
msgid ""
"The selected plan places each operating gap on its own proportional "
"ruler, while the ledger keeps quantities in their original units. The "
"figure reports one selected feasible benchmark plan, not a causal "
"diagnosis or a management order."
msgstr "所选方案把每项经营缺口置于各自的比例标尺上，同时在明细中保留数量的原始单位。图中报告的是一个所选可行标杆方案，而不是因果诊断或管理命令。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:554 483a51bdcc1a4d6da4aaa8121ddf8040
msgid ""
"The left panel makes unlike dimensions comparable without pretending that"
" they share physical units. The right panel returns to observed and "
"target quantities that a manager can audit. Reading both panels together "
"prevents a common mistake: a dimensionless score is useful for "
"comparison, but operational interpretation still belongs at the variable "
"level."
msgstr ""
"左图使不同维度可以比较，却不假定它们共享物理单位；右图则回到管理者可以审计的观测量和目标量。两图结合可以避免一个常见错误：无量纲得分便于比较，但经营解释仍应落实到变量层面。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:560 be1887748a1c498b9154f6792ecc4ac6
msgid ""
"There is no contradiction when the three orientations classify a plan "
"differently. Input orientation asks only whether resources can be reduced"
" while services are maintained; output orientation asks the corresponding"
" service-expansion question. A one-sided score of one must not be "
"reported as an unconditional claim of strong efficiency."
msgstr ""
"三种导向对同一方案作出不同分类并不矛盾。投入导向只问在维持服务的同时能否减少资源；产出导向则问相应的服务扩张问题。单侧得分为 1，不得被报告为无条件的强有效结论。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:566 e9034d2b0ab54c65a0a73e390ed42fd9
msgid "The joint result exposes the operational evidence directly:"
msgstr "联合结果直接揭示经营证据："

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:575 a5b65cb60dd64a9686955f953a2bdc50
msgid ""
"Those original-unit values are usually more useful to a manager than the "
"aggregate score alone. They also let the reader reconstruct the input and"
" output accounts instead of trusting a black-box ranking."
msgstr ""
"这些以原始单位表示的数值通常比单独一个汇总得分更有助于管理决策。它们也使读者能够重构投入账户和产出账户，而不必盲信黑箱排序。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:579 39243393029a441fabaa6c4cde81fb5c
msgid ""
"The table also warns against treating orientation as a robustness race. "
"The input, output, and joint columns need not preserve the same ranking "
"because they value different improvements. A ranking change is evidence "
"that the managerial mandate matters, not evidence that one formulation "
"must be discarded."
msgstr "该表还提醒我们，不能把导向当成一场稳健性竞赛。投入、产出和联合三列不一定保持相同排序，因为它们评价不同的改进。排序变化说明评价所依据的管理任务会影响结果，并不表示必须抛弃某种形式。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:585 cf5d28c392fe4cbb89c07e7cd895e2cc
msgid "Targets are evidence, not prescriptions"
msgstr "目标方案是证据，不是处方"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:587 f2a8d35988904022b0a5d20af25dc748
msgid ""
"An SBM score can be well determined while several peer combinations or "
"targets attain it. Software returns one optimal plan; another equally "
"good plan may identify different peers or distribute improvements "
"differently. The risk is greatest on the side omitted from an oriented "
"objective, but alternative optima can also affect objective-side targets."
msgstr ""
"SBM "
"得分可能确定得很好，但多个活跃参照单元组合或目标方案都能达到该得分。软件返回其中一个最优方案；另一同样好的方案可能识别不同的活跃参照单元，或以不同方式分配改进。导向目标函数未纳入的一侧风险最大，但多个最优解也可能影响目标侧的目标量。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:593 76e0ef860d5c427280fe819e8a0d236f
msgid ""
"A careful report therefore separates the score from the selected plan. "
"Report the orientation, the proportional input and output accounts "
"relevant to it, the most important original-unit targets, and whether "
"alternative optima were examined. A target is evidence that a plan is "
"feasible under the fitted technology. It is not automatically a budget, "
"quota, forecast, or causal effect of a management intervention. Peer "
"weights describe a benchmark construction; they do not prove that copying"
" a named peer will produce the same outcome."
msgstr "因此，谨慎的报告应把得分与所选方案分开。需要报告导向、与之相关的投入和产出比例账户、最重要的原始单位目标，并说明是否检验了多个最优解。目标方案提供的是某一方案在拟合技术下可行的证据，却不自动成为预算、配额、预测或管理干预的因果效应。参照权重描述标杆如何构造，并不能证明照搬某个具名活跃参照单元就会产生同样结果。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:602 e23dd870313c4c798804621ba03f77fe
msgid "Conditions that keep the comparison meaningful"
msgstr "保持比较有意义的条件"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:604 b7d857ae2fef4fc4b585fd45c5966ff2
msgid ""
"Standard SBM requires strictly positive inputs and outputs because "
"observed values appear in the denominators. A zero makes relative slack "
"undefined, and a negative denominator reverses the interpretation of "
"improvement. Adding a small constant or translating a column changes the "
"estimand and may change rankings. SBM is unit invariant, but it is not "
"translation invariant."
msgstr ""
"标准 SBM "
"要求投入和产出严格为正，因为观测值出现在分母中。零值会使相对松弛量无定义，负分母会颠倒改进的解释。增加小常数或平移整列会改变被估量，也可能改变排序。SBM"
" 具有单位不变性，但不具有平移不变性。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:610 c2ec16db6a6541afa343ae69c02cf6d9
msgid ""
"Returns to scale and the reference population are substantive choices for"
" the Additive and SBM accounts. CRS allows proportional scaling of "
"observed activities; VRS compares convex combinations at represented "
"operating scales. Neither is universally more conservative, so the "
"analyst should choose from the production setting and report the choice. "
"The named RAM account above is the deliberate exception: its source "
"profile is VRS and its range population matches its reference population."
msgstr ""
"规模报酬与参照总体是加法模型和 SBM 账户中的实质性选择。CRS 允许观测生产活动按比例缩放；VRS "
"则在代表性经营规模上比较凸组合。二者都不普遍更保守，分析者应依据生产环境选择并报告。上述具名 RAM 账户是有意设置的例外：其来源设定为 "
"VRS，极差总体与参照总体相同。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:618 aba1fe89bda7465ea40a82e16c1b9291
msgid ""
"Likewise, the frontier represents only the observations declared eligible"
" as comparators. Removing the evaluated unit, restricting comparison to a"
" group, or using another period can change feasibility as well as the "
"score. In the standard non-oriented positive-data account, a feasible "
"score of one implies zero normalized slacks algebraically. An external "
"reference can nevertheless change whether the observed plan belongs to "
"the technology, whether the comparison is feasible, and what an "
"efficiency classification means. Those conditions must be re-established "
"rather than borrowed from a self-inclusive appraisal."
msgstr ""
"同样，前沿只代表被声明为合格比较对象的观测。剔除被评价单元、把比较限制在一个群组内或采用另一时期，都可能改变可行性和得分。在标准非导向正值账户中，可行得分为"
" 1 "
"在代数上意味着归一化松弛量为零。但外部参照仍会改变观测方案是否属于该技术、比较是否可行，以及效率分类具有什么含义。这些条件必须重新确立，不能从包含被评价单元自身的评价中直接借用。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/04-sbm.md:628 57c959589a56448f8b519d452e0b944b
msgid ""
"Finally, ordinary SBM assumes desirable outputs and the standard convex "
"production account. Undesirable outputs, networks, signed data, super-"
"efficiency, and productivity change require their own technologies or "
"measures. Keeping those boundaries explicit lets SBM do what it does "
"best: translate uneven resource excesses and service shortfalls into an "
"auditable operating-performance account matched to management's actual "
"mandate."
msgstr ""
"最后，普通 SBM 假设合意产出与标准凸生产账户。非合意产出、网络、有符号数据、超效率和生产率变化需要各自的技术或测度。明确这些边界，才能让 "
"SBM 发挥所长：把不均衡的资源冗余与服务不足转化为一套可审计、且与管理层实际任务相匹配的经营绩效账户。"
